The main metric is the total energy together with its single terms. Further metrics are hard-constraint violations (which must be zero), the share of infeasible runs, the number of plants placed, deviation from the target proportions, monthly flowering coverage and runtime. For each run the relative improvement $I=(E_{\mathrm{greedy}}-E_{\mathrm{SA}})/E_{\mathrm{greedy}}$ over its own greedy start is summarized by median and interquartile range and tested per area with a one-sided paired Wilcoxon signed-rank test, with a Holm correction across areas. Insertion orders are compared on matched seeds. Because only three geometries are tested, conclusions are limited to these scenarios. No expert-made reference plan is available, so the plans are also rendered as maps, colored by bloom month and scaled by height, and reviewed with the supervisor. The main limitation is that the results depend on the chosen rules, traits and weights, which is why the sensitivity experiments are part of the evaluation. A second limitation is that rules based on few plants, such as the 8 structural plants of list C, are noisy and affected by the area edges, and a third is that the plant count is fixed before annealing.

